## Medium Findings

### MED-01: Session Token Predictability

| Attribute | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Severity | Medium |
| CVSS | 5.3 |
| Location | api.medsync.health |
| Status | Remediated |

**Description**: Session tokens used insufficiently random seed, potentially allowing prediction after observing multiple tokens.

**Remediation**: Migrated to cryptographically secure random number generator (CSPRNG) for all token generation. Remediated December 10, 2024.

**Verification**: Retest confirmed fix on December 16, 2024.

---

### MED-02: Insufficient Rate Limiting on Password Reset

| Attribute | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Severity | Medium |
| CVSS | 5.1 |
| Location | app.medsync.health/auth/reset |
| Status | Remediated |

**Description**: Password reset endpoint allowed unlimited requests, enabling user enumeration and potential account lockout abuse.

**Remediation**: Implemented progressive rate limiting: 5 requests/hour per email, CAPTCHA after 3 requests. Remediated December 8, 2024.

**Verification**: Retest confirmed fix on December 16, 2024.

---

### MED-03: Verbose Error Messages in Production

| Attribute | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Severity | Medium |
| CVSS | 4.7 |
| Location | api.medsync.health (multiple endpoints) |
| Status | Remediated |

**Description**: Stack traces and internal error details exposed in production API responses, providing information useful to attackers.

**Remediation**: Implemented global error handler to sanitize all production error responses. Remediated December 12, 2024.

**Verification**: Retest confirmed fix on December 17, 2024.

